name: Link Analysis insider threat showcase
tagline: "A seeded insider-threat Link Analysis demo - a leaver's bulk reads and mail to a personal domain, access creep granted by one manager and two employees approving each other's expenses, planted among 3 000 invented employees with benign look-alikes"
description: "The security, HR and internal-investigations insider-threat Link Analysis demo as a Space Template, Basic tier. Six synthetic feeds (employee, access_grant, access_daily, email_external, expense, vendor_change; 12 months landed from 2025-10-01 in data/inbox, the next month in data/staged; 3 000 invented employees known by id only, about 12 200 access grants, 106 000 DAILY read counts per employee and system - never record-level - 29 000 days of external mail aggregated per employee and domain, 18 000 expense claims and 570 vendor master changes) are landed by six Collectors and Pipelines. The insider_links Job folds them into ONE link Dataset (src, dst, kind, ts, amount, event_date, via) of six link kinds; the insider_screen_links Job derives the three insider-risk screens the saved views read. Planted stories (ground truth: tools/gen-la-insider-data.ground-truth.json; pinned by InsiderLinksJobGoldenTest and tools/gen-la-insider-data.test.mjs): a customer account specialist who gives notice, then reads about 20 times their normal customer records for three weeks and mails 1.2 GB to a personal domain; an operations manager (EMP-0007) who grants payroll and treasury access to 4 of their reports with no ticket, one of whom then changes a vendor's bank details; two account managers who approve each other's expenses 40 times, just under the 500 limit, mostly at weekends. Benign look-alikes that must not join a story: a migration engineer's ticketed bulk read, an employee moved into payroll and granted access with a ticket, and a sales team lead approving a busy field team. Three saved views. Basic tier: runs on every edition, Basic included. Advanced tier, in the same template and inert on Basic: Demo Users and roles (config/demo-users.toon, roles.toon: insider.analyst lead, insider.manager second approver, insider.reviewer read-only, insider.outsider not a member, admin), four-eyes above a fan-out of 2000 and Drafts (link-analysis.toon), the insider_ticketless_grant_counts and insider_ticketless_grant_alerts Jobs and the Alert Rule insider_finance_grant_without_ticket (a grant without a ticket to a finance system: on the shipped data it counts the 8 payroll and treasury grants EMP-0007 made to 4 reports, out of 258 grants without a ticket to any system; the employee moved into payroll with a ticket is not counted; the Alert names a count, never a person; unarmed on Basic). Investigations, members, an Entity List, a Case, a held four-eyes expand and a Draft are runtime state: run `node tools/seed-la-insider.mjs --apply` on an Advanced or Preview build with Demo Auth. Synthetic data only: every person, system, vendor and mail domain is invented."
minEdition: basic
icon: heroicons_outline:identification
contents[7]: "6 Collectors + Pipelines + Datasets (12 months landed, 1 month staged)", "insider_links Job + Dataset (6 link kinds, via) and the insider_screen_links Dataset of three insider-risk screens", "3 saved views (leaver exfiltration, access creep, mutual approvals)", "3 planted stories with benign look-alikes", "Ground truth and golden tests in the repository", "Advanced tier: 5 Demo Users + role table, four-eyes (inert on Basic)", "Advanced tier: Alert Rule on a grant without a ticket to a finance system (counts Job + evaluate Job, unarmed on Basic)"
